<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karelian Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1923–1940, 1956–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Karelian ASSR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karelian Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic was an autonomous republic of the Russian SFSR with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrozavodsk">Petrozavodsk</a>. In 1940, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a>, it was combined with territory ceded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> to form the Karelo-Finnish SSR, a full union republic. In 1956 it was downgraded again to an autonomous republic, and it is now the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karelian-assr.jpg" alt="Karelian Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Urmas assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Karelian_ASSR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
